    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a clear emphasis on exploiting favorable pitching matchups to bolster our efficiency. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) and **Jackson Merrill** (71.66) headline our lineup as the premier starts of the day. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from an exceptional matchup against Burnes (xERA 5.41), where his strong platoon advantage and batting order stability create a high ceiling for run production. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** thrives against Alcantara, as his elite profile against right-handed pitching and a favorable SP xERA allow him to maximize scoring potential in the five-by-five format. **Gunnar Henderson** (66.59) remains a mandatory start despite a formidable matchup against Misiorowski; while the opposing xERA of 2.32 is a significant hurdle, **Gunnar Henderson**\u2019s underlying power metrics and park factors provide enough cushion to keep him in the elite tier of our daily distribution.\n\nStrategic lineup construction required a difficult decision regarding the utility spot and the remaining bench depth. **Josh Jung** (41.97) was the strongest candidate left on the bench, narrowly missing the cut behind **Coby Mayo** (44.14). While **Josh Jung** projects well, the efficiency optimizer favored **Coby Mayo** due to the latter's slightly higher projected volume in RBI opportunities, despite the challenge posed by Misiorowski. We continue to monitor the status of **Kyle Tucker**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, and **Andy Pages**, whose absences from the active roster necessitate high performance from depth pieces like **Sam Antonacci** (62.92) and **Heliot Ramos** (66.03). Both outfielders are in excellent positions to provide much-needed stolen base and run support today.\n\nCaution is advised regarding **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (48.21), who faces the daunting task of squaring off against deGrom. While his order placement at #2 provides structural value, the matchup against an elite arm limits his upside significantly, keeping him in the marginal start category. Additionally, we are tracking confirmed lineups for **Gunnar Henderson** and **Coby Mayo**; should their assumed batting positions shift downward, their efficiency scores will require immediate re-evaluation. With **Nasim Nunez** (49.84) providing necessary versatility at MI, we are prioritizing floor stability over high-variance swings while we await the return of injured assets such as **Jordan Westburg**, **Jacob Wilson**, and the rest of our developmental talent like **Liam Hicks**, **Luis Lara**, **Franklin Arias**, **Tommy White**, and **Henry Bolte**.",
